          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE:HIGH",
              "DATADOG_CONFIDENCE_REASON:Source: attacker-controlled `taskAction` via `stream.defaultReadObject()` during Java deserialization. Sink: command execution at `Process p = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(taskAction);` (line 69). Dataflow: deserialized `taskAction` → validation (`startsWith(\"sleep\"/\"ping\")` and `length()\u003c22`) → direct use as the full argument to `exec`. Sanitization: only weak prefix/length checks; no quoting/escaping or allowlisted exact command + arguments, so metacharacters/OS parsing can still lead to command injection/RCE. Conclusion: true positive."
            ]
          },
          "ruleId": "datadog/java-cmdi",
          "ruleIndex": 4,
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "Source: attacker-controlled `taskAction` via `stream.defaultReadObject()` during Java deserialization. Sink: command execution at `Process p = Runtime.getRuntime().exec(taskAction);` (line 69). Dataflow: deserialized `taskAction` → validation (`startsWith(\"sleep\"/\"ping\")` and `length()\u003c22`) → direct use as the full argument to `exec`. Sanitization: only weak prefix/length checks; no quoting/escaping or allowlisted exact command + arguments, so metacharacters/OS parsing can still lead to command injection/RCE. Conclusion: true positive."
          },
          "locations": [
